Cell[TextData[{
 "Pero las reglas ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["21", 
        RowBox[{"4", ",", "1"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "21_{4,1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1f31bd54-fa1a-4277-96d3-ac669aec3683"],
 " ni ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["13", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "1"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "13_{3,1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4d81ad23-29b2-4751-9904-aaa5e9d662ee"],
 " no pertenencen a la lista de comportamientos unicos, sin embargo, podemos \
aplicar la funci\[OAcute]n ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "InverseRules"], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "ba543329-eb4d-43f0-854d-cf9e37220820"],
 " para encontrar el representante de ese ese comportamiento y descubirir de \
donde viene here dado ese patr\[OAcute]n. Haciendo esto, Descubrimos que la \
regla ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["31", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", "1"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "31_{5,1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "38c7d50c-d2d7-447e-a8ca-573453be2250"],
 " tiene el siguiente patr\[OAcute]n aplicando las dos posibles funciones. \
Este proceso finaliza hasta que no es posible realizar ninguna de las 2 \
operaciones."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9905902911084642`*^9, 3.990590456588768*^9}, 
   3.9905907846714773`*^9, {3.9905941368534927`*^9, 
   3.9905941942143373`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bdc316c8-7e96-46dd-8dad-\
184d155c7b9d"],

